WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
- All right, we've got one last story.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.030
I hope it's gonna make you smile.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.120
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.989
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.989 --> 00:00:06.690
(audience applauding)

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.900
So, last year was a record
setting year for concerts.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.830
No joke.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.750
More tickets were sold last year

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.548
than in any year in history.

00:00:14.548 --> 00:00:15.840
(audience clapping)

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.070
One thing we truly missed

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.530
was getting together and enjoying music.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.520
Well, there's a charity

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.470
making sure veterans and their families

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.220
get to take in live shows all
for free, which is so cool.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.630
It's called Vet Tix,

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.090
and we have the Chief
Strategy Officer, Steve,

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.200
on the line right now.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.210
He also happens to be a veteran himself.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.797
Thank you so much for your service, Steve.

00:00:34.797 --> 00:00:36.480
(audience cheering)

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.490
I'm gonna lead with that.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.340
And then also, I love this
idea. Where did this come from?

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.490
- Well, this idea came from
our founder, Mike Focareto.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.630
He's a Navy veteran.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.320
And back in 2008, he was at
the Super Bowl here in Phoenix,

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.440
and he looked around and
saw pockets of empty seats.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.867
And he thought, "What a waste.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:57.660
How can I get veterans and service members

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.780
and their families into
these seats that go unused,

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.690
not only at sporting events,
but at concerts as well?"

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.310
So, he created Vet Tix.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.710
Fast forward 15 years,

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.320
and now we have over 2 million members

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.849
and we've distributed
over 15 million tickets.

00:01:12.849 --> 00:01:13.682
(audience applauding)

00:01:13.682 --> 00:01:14.820
And these tickets are donated

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.870
by performers, promoters, entertainers,

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.720
and Kelly, a lot of our Vet Tix members

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.470
have attended concerts
seeing you through Vet Tix.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.420
- Oh my gosh! That's awesome.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.550
So, this has a special meaning

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.370
for each person who gets
to go to a show, right?

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:36.480
- Absolutely. I spent 32
years in the Marine Corps.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.550
I retired as a colonel.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.090
And when you're in the military
or you're a first responder,

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.150
you miss time away from your family

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.770
and you miss a lot of events.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.720
So, if we can use these tickets

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.420
to send these service
members and first responders

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.880
and their families to these
concerts and other events

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.690
as a way to make up for that
lost time and create memories,

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.100
then it's a great thing.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.890
And you know, Kelly, music heals,

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.225
and it really helps create memories

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:08.700
and helps people through
the challenges and struggles

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.430
they've had in serving in the
military or their community.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.960
The cool thing is,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.030
is that these tickets are usually donated

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.260
in sections or blocks.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.020
So, these members are at these events

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.840
with other service members
or first responders

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.680
as a way to make new friends,
create bonds and new memories.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.700
- This is such a cool thing

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.470
that you've done for all these people.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.400
Steve, thank you so much.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.115
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:31.115 --> 00:02:33.780
(audience applauding)

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.160
And that's not all, Steve.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.720
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.000
makers of G2, the the go-to
pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.800
want to help you provide more veterans

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.180
with concert experiences,

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.220
so they're gonna give Vet
Tix a thousand dollars.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.225
How's that sound?

00:02:45.225 --> 00:02:47.160
(audience clapping)

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.270
- That's amazing.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.630
Thank you so much, to you and to Pilot.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.190
Because with that donation,

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.930
even more veterans and service members

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.420
are gonna create even more memories

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.070
than they've already experienced.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.750
So, thank you so much.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.130
- Aw, man, that's all because of you

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:03.480
and this domino effect that you started.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.100
Thank you, Steve.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.875
All right, thank you to everybody.

00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:10.380
All our guests this hour,
Pink, Justin Derrico, and Tim.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.213
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:11.213 --> 00:03:13.219
And if it's not, just listen
to Pink. You'll feel better.

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:14.052
(audience clapping)

